WEBVTT

00:06.630 --> 00:08.580
Starting today, I'm a second year.

00:16.670 --> 00:18.960
The walk to school is the same as it always is.

00:21.380 --> 00:22.960
When I swing by the convenience store,

00:22.960 --> 00:25.710
the clerk gets startled like she always does.

00:28.170 --> 00:29.250
Achoo!

00:30.790 --> 00:35.460
When I sneeze, the people around me show
their surprise at my existence with their piercing stares.

00:36.710 --> 00:38.670
Even though I moved up a grade,

00:38.920 --> 00:42.960
I can't say my world has changed one bit.

00:44.580 --> 00:47.330
I'm just as invisible as ever.

00:48.420 --> 00:52.540
The new school year means a class change.

00:53.880 --> 00:56.420
A new class makes your heart race,

00:56.750 --> 01:00.130
and before entering the classroom,
you might take a few deep breaths.

01:00.380 --> 01:01.830
At least, that's what I gather.

01:03.250 --> 01:07.710
Even though my class is changing,
that basically changes nothing for me.

01:08.960 --> 01:14.460
Like always, no one will notice me,
talk to me, or look for me.

01:14.790 --> 01:15.420
Look!

01:16.790 --> 01:17.920
I can't see…

01:26.790 --> 01:27.750
<b>Class 2-1</b>

01:28.750 --> 01:30.630
<b>Junta Shiraishi</b>

01:28.750 --> 01:30.630
<b>Yuma Sudo</b>

01:29.670 --> 01:31.540
Class 2-1, huh?

01:36.790 --> 01:37.920
<b>Seating Chart</b>

01:37.170 --> 01:38.670
Where's my seat?

01:39.250 --> 01:40.290
<b>Tamao Taira</b>

01:39.250 --> 01:40.290
<b>Hazuki Kudo</b>

01:41.210 --> 01:43.080
Shiraishi-kun, your seat

01:43.080 --> 01:45.290
is in the very back by the window.

01:46.790 --> 01:48.130
Lucky!

01:48.960 --> 01:50.630
It's like you're a main character.

01:52.830 --> 01:55.040
Good morning, Shiraishi-kun.

01:55.500 --> 01:57.420
G-good morning.

01:58.130 --> 01:59.670
We're in the same class.

02:01.170 --> 02:05.130
Despite the class change, Kubo-san found me.

02:07.920 --> 02:10.710
Please, just for a moment

02:10.710 --> 02:14.750
Let the time freeze

02:16.920 --> 02:20.330
When did it start?

02:20.330 --> 02:24.000
I cannot remember

02:24.830 --> 02:28.630
Who actually cares?

02:28.630 --> 02:31.380
"It doesn't matter"

02:31.920 --> 02:34.960
Laughing or shedding tears

02:34.960 --> 02:39.080
Whenever we realized

02:39.540 --> 02:45.040
Or too persistent to take in sometime

02:46.380 --> 02:56.290
Ready? And go as the traffic light changes (As we are)

02:56.290 --> 03:00.250
No words needed (as far as we can be)

03:00.420 --> 03:03.380
we can surely make it

03:03.380 --> 03:07.040
Even if it wasn't dramatic

03:07.210 --> 03:10.920
Even if it was boring and I was moaning

03:11.210 --> 03:16.130
I'll remember this day

03:16.580 --> 03:17.580
When? I don't know

03:18.130 --> 03:21.830
I don't need no romantic words

03:22.000 --> 03:25.420
I just want one thing

03:25.500 --> 03:28.170
Let the time freeze

03:28.170 --> 03:32.080
Just for a moment...

03:32.580 --> 03:34.500
The words fell

03:38.040 --> 03:39.710
This is surprising, isn't it?

03:39.210 --> 03:43.790
<b>Episode 9: New School Year and Class Change</b>

03:39.960 --> 03:43.330
I thought the teacher would assign seats
based on our roll call numbers,

03:43.330 --> 03:45.750
but they aren't organized that way on the seating chart.

03:45.750 --> 03:51.040
<b>Seating Chart</b>

03:45.750 --> 03:51.040
<b>Junta Shiraishi   Nagisa Kubo</b>

03:45.750 --> 03:51.040
<b>Tamao Taira</b>

03:45.750 --> 03:51.040
<b>Hazuki Kudo</b>

03:46.170 --> 03:48.960
You thought seats would be based
on roll call numbers, didn't ya?

03:49.670 --> 03:51.040
Surprise!

03:51.250 --> 03:53.580
Our teacher and his shenanigans!

03:53.580 --> 03:55.500
Y-yeah.

03:55.710 --> 03:57.290
Ah, Nagisa!

03:57.290 --> 03:58.330
Kubocchi!

03:59.000 --> 04:01.040
Hazuki! Tama!

04:01.540 --> 04:03.830
I'm so glad we're in the same class!

04:03.830 --> 04:04.630
Same!

04:04.630 --> 04:06.130
This is awesome!

04:22.080 --> 04:24.500
All right, I got a question for you, Shiraishi-kun.

04:24.830 --> 04:25.460
Huh?

04:25.750 --> 04:28.130
Where is my seat?

04:29.380 --> 04:31.170
I only looked for my se-

04:31.170 --> 04:32.420
I'll give you a hint.

04:33.500 --> 04:36.170
It's the seat you just looked at.

04:36.920 --> 04:38.000
I wasn't looking at anything.

04:38.540 --> 04:40.170
Then I'll give you a bonus hint.

04:40.710 --> 04:42.170
The bunny pouch.

04:46.630 --> 04:47.920
The seat beside mine?

04:50.380 --> 04:51.210
Correct!

04:53.580 --> 04:55.210
We're seat neighbors for another year.

04:55.630 --> 05:00.460
Wait, no. Third years don't have a class change.

05:00.920 --> 05:02.710
We're neighbors until graduation.

05:03.790 --> 05:05.130
Yep, we are.

05:06.420 --> 05:08.880
Hmm? Why're you looking over there?

05:09.380 --> 05:11.670
The sky is just so pretty.

05:13.750 --> 05:15.000
It really is!

05:20.580 --> 05:26.210
No one notices me, talks to me,
or looks for me. Such is my life.

05:26.670 --> 05:29.290
But Kubo-san finds me.

05:29.830 --> 05:32.500
She tells me good morning.

05:32.790 --> 05:37.540
So many things I could've never
imagined happen when I'm with Kubo-san.

05:37.920 --> 05:40.290
Anyway, what I'm saying is…

05:40.960 --> 05:44.170
Let's have loads of fun as second years!

05:46.130 --> 05:46.830
Yeah.

05:49.920 --> 05:51.540
Why are you surprised?

05:52.500 --> 05:53.380
Well…

05:54.290 --> 05:58.380
I never thought of school as something that's fun.

05:59.670 --> 06:00.750
It's nothing.

06:01.040 --> 06:02.920
What, I wanna know!

06:03.210 --> 06:06.500
I was surprised by the words
that came out of my own mouth.

06:06.750 --> 06:10.420
But Kubo-san would laugh if I told her,
so I'm keeping it to myself.

06:13.920 --> 06:14.500
Okay,

06:14.500 --> 06:18.130
let's celebrate how lucky
we were to end up in the same class!

06:18.380 --> 06:19.960
Let's have a great year together!

06:20.330 --> 06:22.170
Yeah!

06:22.710 --> 06:25.290
Let's enjoy every day together again!

06:25.670 --> 06:27.210
Yeah, for sure!

06:27.500 --> 06:32.250
I was seriously wondering what I'd do
if I was the only one in a different class.

06:32.580 --> 06:36.830
Yeah. But it's such a relief we
all ended up in the same class.

06:38.630 --> 06:40.670
Speaking of which, what about Shiraishi?

06:40.670 --> 06:42.540
I guess he's in a different class.

06:42.880 --> 06:44.420
He's in our class.

06:44.710 --> 06:47.540
He was?! I didn't notice him!

06:47.540 --> 06:51.540
As usual, Nagisa has mad Shiraishi spotting skills.

06:52.040 --> 06:54.000
It's because we're seat neighbors.

06:54.460 --> 06:58.540
Well, I'm not sure I'd notice him even
if he was sitting next to me.

06:58.830 --> 07:00.000
Same.

07:00.380 --> 07:02.670
Oh, really?

07:03.380 --> 07:08.380
Anyway, we get to have a blast together
all the way until graduation!

07:08.380 --> 07:10.830
Do you only think about having fun?

07:10.830 --> 07:14.420
C'mon, let's have a ball! M'kay?

07:14.420 --> 07:15.830
All right, all right.

07:15.830 --> 07:17.330
Yay! Awesome!

07:18.580 --> 07:20.130
I'm home!

07:24.210 --> 07:25.920
Oh, you're home.

07:26.500 --> 07:27.750
Welcome back!

07:28.500 --> 07:30.580
How was the first day of the new school year?

07:31.210 --> 07:33.580
Hazuki and Tama are in the same class as me.

07:33.920 --> 07:35.330
That's wonderful!

07:35.920 --> 07:36.580
Uh-huh.

07:36.920 --> 07:39.920
And? What about that boy? Is he in your class too?

07:40.250 --> 07:43.040
Huh? Shiraishi-kun? Why do you ask?

07:43.040 --> 07:48.580
Because he's one of the three kiddos I know. So is he?

07:49.790 --> 07:51.170
We're in the same class.

07:52.380 --> 07:54.290
That's great, isn't it?

07:55.500 --> 07:56.420
Not really.

07:56.710 --> 07:58.170
There you go again!

08:02.830 --> 08:06.420
Okay! Today we're choosing
everyone's student committees!

08:07.290 --> 08:08.920
Student committees, huh?

08:09.250 --> 08:09.830
Hey.

08:11.750 --> 08:13.710
Which committee are you choosing?

08:14.420 --> 08:17.420
Me? I guess whatever's left over.

08:17.420 --> 08:19.040
Whatever's left over?

08:19.630 --> 08:22.880
Well, even if I raise my hand,
the teacher won't call on me.

08:22.880 --> 08:23.880
Ah…

08:24.210 --> 08:28.210
There isn't a committee I'm interested in, anyway.
I'm cool with whatever.

08:28.420 --> 08:29.460
Hmm.

08:29.750 --> 08:33.130
Last year you were in the
Environmental Committee, right?

08:33.130 --> 08:34.710
You took care of the flower beds.

08:35.170 --> 08:36.920
You're perceptive.

08:37.250 --> 08:38.460
I noticed!

08:38.710 --> 08:42.380
The flower beds that don't have weeds
despite no one taking care of them

08:42.380 --> 08:44.250
became one of the school's seven wonders.

08:44.460 --> 08:46.210
One of the school's seven wonders?!

08:47.250 --> 08:52.880
Why don't the flowers wither even
though no one's been tending to them?

08:52.880 --> 08:54.920
It's truly a mystery!

08:55.580 --> 08:57.290
I-is that so?

08:58.290 --> 09:00.130
Do you like the Environmental Committee?

09:00.920 --> 09:02.710
Well, not in particular.

09:03.130 --> 09:07.500
Doing stuff like watering flowers, pulling weeds,
and picking up litter is a drag.

09:08.460 --> 09:09.330
But…

09:10.250 --> 09:14.330
I did feel fulfilled when the flowers
I took care of bloomed.

09:14.790 --> 09:17.420
Hey, look! The flowers are blooming!

09:17.710 --> 09:19.460
They're so pretty!

09:20.000 --> 09:24.630
I'm invisible and rarely noticed by others.

09:25.080 --> 09:33.500
Maybe that's why I remember feeling so happy that
everyone noticed and admired my blooming flowers.

09:25.290 --> 09:28.000
Ah, they're so lovely!

09:28.000 --> 09:29.170
They are!

09:34.920 --> 09:40.580
Even if I wanted to be in that committee again,
I won't have a say in the matter.

09:41.710 --> 09:45.460
All right, next up, who wants to be in
the Environmental Committee?

09:45.460 --> 09:48.290
I'm the advisor for this committee, by the way!

09:48.500 --> 09:51.080
Being on that committee's a pain in the neck.

09:51.250 --> 09:55.790
Pulling weeds and watering flowers
kinda cuts into your break time.

09:59.500 --> 10:00.250
I do!

10:03.330 --> 10:04.500
Oh!

10:06.290 --> 10:08.580
So you want to join the Environmental Committee, huh?

10:08.580 --> 10:11.420
It felt like my heart was breaking
when no one raised their hand.

10:12.460 --> 10:14.210
Does anyone else want to join?

10:14.460 --> 10:17.830
There is some manual labor involved,
so it would be nice if a boy would join.

10:18.830 --> 10:22.080
Kubo-san wanted to join the Environmental Committee.

10:22.460 --> 10:23.580
I didn't see that coming.

10:23.580 --> 10:25.170
Oh, sir.

10:25.460 --> 10:27.790
Shiraishi-kun also raised his hand.

10:30.130 --> 10:31.750
You don't care which one you join, right?

10:32.830 --> 10:33.580
Huh?

10:34.000 --> 10:35.460
Is that right,

10:36.250 --> 10:37.790
Shiraishi?

10:38.630 --> 10:40.920
I apologize for not noticing you raised your hand!

10:40.920 --> 10:42.170
Uh, ah…

10:42.630 --> 10:43.250
Kubo-sa...

10:43.250 --> 10:46.630
Come to think of it, you were on
the committee last year too.

10:48.080 --> 10:51.420
The flower beds were always lovely thanks to you.

10:51.420 --> 10:53.420
I'm counting on you this year too.

10:56.330 --> 10:57.080
Yes, sir.

11:00.750 --> 11:03.540
All right. It seems like no one else wants to join,

11:03.540 --> 11:06.500
so these two will make up our Environmental Committee.

11:10.710 --> 11:12.580
You look happy.

11:13.330 --> 11:15.710
You wanted to be on the Environmental Committee?

11:16.420 --> 11:17.290
Hmm,

11:17.580 --> 11:18.880
I was meh on it.

11:18.880 --> 11:19.500
Oh?

11:19.790 --> 11:21.210
But…

11:21.670 --> 11:23.380
Wh-what?

11:25.710 --> 11:29.000
Didn't you put your socks
on inside out the other day too?

11:29.380 --> 11:32.000
I overslept and had to hurry!

11:47.790 --> 11:51.000
Have you tried the new chocolate melon bread
that came out recently?

11:51.000 --> 11:52.750
I haven't tried it yet!

11:52.750 --> 11:54.750
They sold out stupid fast!

11:55.000 --> 11:57.460
Snagging one is a real battle!

11:58.080 --> 12:01.830
Hey, look! The flowers are blooming!

12:01.830 --> 12:03.710
They're so pretty!

12:04.420 --> 12:07.170
Shiraishi-kun takes care of that flower bed.

12:15.750 --> 12:18.540
I kinda liked the idea of it.

12:19.330 --> 12:22.830
That's unusual. Most people think it's a sucky committee.

12:22.830 --> 12:27.920
Oh, but you're more experienced
with the committee's duties,

12:28.880 --> 12:32.170
so teach me all the ins and outs, senpai.

12:34.170 --> 12:35.040
Sen-

12:37.000 --> 12:41.000
<b>Environmental</b>

12:37.000 --> 12:41.000
<b>Committee:</b>

12:37.000 --> 12:41.000
<b>2 members</b>

12:37.000 --> 12:41.000
<b>Shiraishi  Kubo</b>

12:37.000 --> 12:41.000
<b>I'm happy</b>

12:41.960 --> 12:44.830
You're on a committee with a girl? Lucky!

12:45.210 --> 12:47.330
There are only dudes on the Athletics Committee.

12:47.630 --> 12:50.960
Speaking of committees, Kubo-san is
on the Environmental Committee, right?

12:51.250 --> 12:53.670
Taking care of flowers and whatnot really suits her.

12:54.130 --> 12:56.130
Oh, who was the other person again?

12:56.130 --> 12:58.040
Um, Shiraishi, right?

12:58.380 --> 13:04.420
Ah, Shiraishi. He probably joined because Kubo-san did.

13:04.420 --> 13:05.630
Yeah, that seems likely.

13:07.170 --> 13:10.130
I'm not surprised those guys think that.

13:10.790 --> 13:12.290
Sorry about that.

13:12.830 --> 13:13.790
Kubo-san?

13:14.040 --> 13:17.750
I'm the one who voluntold you.

13:17.750 --> 13:18.920
True that.

13:19.540 --> 13:21.420
Hey, what do you think, Sudo?

13:23.710 --> 13:26.670
Shiraishi was on the
Environmental Committee last year too.

13:26.670 --> 13:28.500
He probably just wanted to do it again, right?

13:28.830 --> 13:33.830
What? Someone actually wants
to be on that craptastic committee?

13:34.290 --> 13:39.170
The teacher complimented his flower beds, and
he seems to have a green thumb, so what's the big deal?

13:39.630 --> 13:43.580
That reminds me, you were on the Environmental
Committee last year too, right?

13:43.580 --> 13:46.210
Didn't your flower beds die?

13:46.460 --> 13:49.540
I thought I took good care of them.

13:49.540 --> 13:52.630
Sudo's a plant murderer.

13:53.040 --> 13:53.920
Can it.

13:55.170 --> 14:00.790
You just thought, "Someone remembered I was
on the Environmental Committee," didn't ya?

14:01.380 --> 14:03.880
Kubo-san, get out of my head!

14:04.880 --> 14:07.670
Have you ever talked to Sudo-kun?

14:07.670 --> 14:09.380
No, I haven't.

14:09.880 --> 14:12.670
Hmm, gotcha, gotcha.

14:13.210 --> 14:15.000
Wh-what?

14:15.460 --> 14:16.710
Nothing.

14:17.500 --> 14:20.630
Our next class is in another room, so I'm going on ahead.

14:21.000 --> 14:21.750
Okay.

14:23.380 --> 14:24.790
Sudo-kun, huh?

14:27.830 --> 14:30.830
Is this the first science lab of the year?

14:31.420 --> 14:33.000
I wonder who will be in my group.

14:33.250 --> 14:35.500
<b>Science Lab</b>

14:44.830 --> 14:47.330
Kubo-san and Sudo-kun are in my group.

14:47.750 --> 14:51.500
We have a few things to go over
for our lab today before we begin.

14:51.500 --> 14:53.250
Open your notebooks and textbooks!

14:53.670 --> 14:55.500
Uh, the chemical formula…

14:59.580 --> 15:01.500
Oh. I wrote that down wrong.

15:04.170 --> 15:05.210
It's gone.

15:05.500 --> 15:07.710
Did he forget to bring an eraser?

15:08.130 --> 15:09.250
What should I do?

15:11.130 --> 15:14.380
I brought five erasers with me today.

15:17.210 --> 15:19.380
But I've never talked to him before.

15:19.380 --> 15:24.670
Well, he must be able to see me since we're right beside
each other.

15:26.960 --> 15:29.040
I made eye contact with Ku-

15:31.580 --> 15:33.460
She's totally plotting something!

15:36.710 --> 15:40.170
Woah! Shiraishi-kun, you have a ton of erasers!

15:41.380 --> 15:42.790
How many do you got?

15:45.710 --> 15:51.250
Uh, ah… Um, five. The teacher said we'd have a quiz,

15:51.460 --> 15:53.290
so I brought extra.

15:56.290 --> 15:57.630
What's with you?

15:57.920 --> 15:59.750
You really came overprepared.

16:01.420 --> 16:03.960
Sudo-kun is laughing.

16:05.130 --> 16:09.540
Hey, Shiraishi. Lend me one
of your erasers. I forgot mine.

16:09.540 --> 16:11.580
Oh, s-sure!

16:13.830 --> 16:14.670
Thanks.

16:15.750 --> 16:20.000
You know, I've been meaning to talk to you.

16:20.750 --> 16:21.710
To me?

16:22.250 --> 16:22.830
Yeah.

16:23.290 --> 16:26.500
I looked after the flower beds last year too,

16:26.830 --> 16:28.790
but nothing I did turned out any good.

16:29.460 --> 16:32.580
Your flower beds were absolutely beautiful,

16:32.880 --> 16:35.500
so I wanted to ask you what your secret is.

16:36.880 --> 16:38.170
Is Junta Shiraishi here?

16:38.580 --> 16:40.460
Well, I haven't seen him today.

16:41.420 --> 16:43.040
Is Shiraishi here today?

16:43.040 --> 16:44.710
I haven't seen him.

16:46.080 --> 16:49.080
Ah, Sudo. I spotted Shiraishi yesterday.

16:49.540 --> 16:50.580
Have you seen him today?

16:50.750 --> 16:51.630
Nope.

16:52.630 --> 16:56.000
In the end, I didn't see him once the entire year.

16:58.630 --> 17:00.580
I couldn't find you.

17:01.040 --> 17:02.670
S-sorry.

17:02.670 --> 17:06.290
So why did you bring five erasers?

17:06.710 --> 17:07.750
Well, I…

17:08.080 --> 17:09.290
Why did I?

17:09.420 --> 17:12.380
What? You're a funny guy.

17:16.670 --> 17:19.330
Sudo-kun is a swell dude.

17:19.830 --> 17:21.880
I'm glad you two got to chat.

17:22.540 --> 17:24.420
Thanks, Kubo-san.

17:25.210 --> 17:26.250
For what?

17:27.670 --> 17:32.170
That was the first time I've been able to enjoy talking
with another person at school besides you.

17:36.380 --> 17:37.290
Kubo-san?

17:38.170 --> 17:41.290
I forgot something. You go on ahead.

17:42.210 --> 17:44.080
Okay, gotcha.

17:49.670 --> 17:51.750
He enjoys talking to me…

17:53.250 --> 17:55.630
<b>Chemistry</b>

17:55.130 --> 17:56.670
He caught me off guard.

18:01.830 --> 18:03.790
I'm a bit thirsty.

18:06.580 --> 18:07.920
I'll get something to drink.

18:08.540 --> 18:11.080
<b>Youthful</b>

18:08.540 --> 18:11.080
<b>Lemon</b>

18:09.460 --> 18:15.540
That reminds me, water often gets left off nutrition labels.

18:15.920 --> 18:21.330
I lowkey relate to water being overlooked
even though it's undeniably there.

18:21.920 --> 18:25.130
Well, that has nothing to do
with whether I'll buy some or not.

18:25.130 --> 18:25.960
Oh.

18:26.080 --> 18:29.670
<b>Youthful</b>

18:26.080 --> 18:29.670
<b>Lemon</b>

18:26.540 --> 18:29.880
A new flavor is out. Lemon, huh?

18:30.330 --> 18:33.000
I can't resist trying out new flavors.

18:36.330 --> 18:38.080
<b>Cold</b>

18:38.790 --> 18:39.210
Oh!

18:39.210 --> 18:40.170
<b>Cold</b>

18:39.750 --> 18:41.710
Found ya, Shiraishi-kun!

18:43.080 --> 18:43.880
Oh…

18:47.250 --> 18:48.210
Water!

18:49.170 --> 18:50.500
Sorry.

18:50.920 --> 18:52.630
Nah, it's all right.

18:53.210 --> 18:55.080
She doesn't seem sorry.

18:55.960 --> 18:58.630
I wanted to buy that new flavor.

18:59.040 --> 19:00.290
New flavor?

19:01.130 --> 19:03.040
This "Youthful Lemon" flavor?

19:03.420 --> 19:06.710
<b>Youthful</b>

19:03.420 --> 19:06.710
<b>Lemon</b>

19:04.080 --> 19:04.750
Yeah.

19:05.210 --> 19:06.460
Oh…

19:09.040 --> 19:12.250
Why is youth lemon flavored?

19:13.500 --> 19:16.000
I feel like youth's flavor would depend on the person.

19:16.250 --> 19:17.250
Definitely.

19:18.290 --> 19:19.130
Hey.

19:22.040 --> 19:25.460
What flavor do you think your youth would be?

19:26.170 --> 19:27.130
Um…

19:27.460 --> 19:29.210
I'd have to think about it.

19:29.210 --> 19:30.580
Aww, c'mon!

19:31.540 --> 19:35.000
My life is a far cry from a fulfilling youth,

19:35.000 --> 19:37.920
so there's no way it'd be lemon.

19:40.580 --> 19:42.170
Mine would be like water.

19:43.290 --> 19:44.630
Like water?

19:45.960 --> 19:47.210
She laughed!

19:49.170 --> 19:50.080
So…

19:52.210 --> 19:54.670
You can be anything you want.

19:59.080 --> 20:07.750
You can be bubbly like a carbonated drink,
refreshing like a sports drink, or fruit flavored.

20:08.210 --> 20:09.750
And there are so many other possibilities.

20:11.750 --> 20:14.210
It's tough to decide since you're so spoiled for choice.

20:16.580 --> 20:18.670
I can be anything?

20:20.080 --> 20:22.290
I hadn't thought of it that way.

20:25.920 --> 20:29.670
But I wonder how you'd get that classic lemon flavor.

20:30.210 --> 20:32.830
I dunno, but…

20:33.330 --> 20:40.920
I have a feeling you'd need a life that's, like,
completely different from mine. I guess…

20:40.920 --> 20:43.420
Shiraishi-kun is staring off into the distance!

20:44.040 --> 20:49.000
Hmm. So you think you'd need a fulfilling youth, right?

20:49.790 --> 20:51.670
For starters, you'd have friends.

20:52.580 --> 20:54.920
You'd have fun at social events and stuff.

20:55.290 --> 20:59.750
Oh! They say your first kiss tastes like lemon,
so maybe it has something to do with that?

21:00.250 --> 21:01.750
What do you think?

21:02.960 --> 21:04.040
Shiraishi-kun?!

21:05.460 --> 21:09.210
The more I hear, the more I think that's out of my reach.

21:09.500 --> 21:11.790
I don't even have friends.

21:12.000 --> 21:12.710
Huh?

21:13.540 --> 21:14.460
Huh?

21:16.290 --> 21:17.460
What about me?

21:19.710 --> 21:22.580
Kubo-san, are we friends?

21:25.750 --> 21:26.790
Kubo-sa...

21:26.790 --> 21:27.580
Oh!

21:30.170 --> 21:31.630
I-I'm sorry.

21:34.130 --> 21:36.210
So I can consider you my friend?

21:40.750 --> 21:43.540
I already thought of us as friends.

21:47.130 --> 21:48.380
Friends…

21:51.580 --> 21:53.500
That sounds fulfilling to me.

22:04.170 --> 22:05.830
Friends, huh?

22:11.130 --> 22:14.500
The school's shadow glows a dark red

22:14.500 --> 22:20.790
I haven't reached the end of my youth

22:21.040 --> 22:26.210
I've experienced a little bit of it, but it'll be over soon

22:26.210 --> 22:30.460
Along with the smiles you give me

22:30.460 --> 22:32.380
It's beautiful

22:32.380 --> 22:35.210
Is it okay to call this a miracle?

22:35.460 --> 22:41.130
I love, love, love these days

22:41.130 --> 22:47.580
But they won't last forever, so I tightly hold on to them

22:47.580 --> 22:51.710
Because we're kids and our spring has just begun

22:51.710 --> 22:55.080
Let's move forward, forward forward, one step at a time

22:55.080 --> 22:58.420
Now, a firm wind faintly blows

22:58.420 --> 23:06.080
I hope our time together at least colors the world a little

23:06.080 --> 23:10.710
What kind of canvas will we paint? What kind of future will we have?

23:10.710 --> 23:14.500
I don't know, but I want to believe

23:13.790 --> 23:18.080
We'll definitely smile and wave at each other

23:14.880 --> 23:17.920
We look forward to tomorrow a little

23:17.920 --> 23:21.630
When we say, "See you later" to each other

23:21.710 --> 23:28.580
With the season's quick passing, our words repeat

23:28.580 --> 23:35.000
Please, please may we be happy!
